entry.description:
The Period-3 Ether Erodes: No Period-3 Wall of Any Width. The primary source reports: **Partial result** for Problem 1, in the kit's reduction of least period 3 to the period-3 ether. Let $F$ be a rule-30 evolution of the columns $p\ge1$ whose column $0$ follows the ether. If at time $t_1$ the columns $1,\dots,k$ ($k\ge1$) and all columns beyond $k+w$ carry the ether, and some column does not, then some column in $1,\dots,k$ leaves the ether at a time $t\le t_1+3w+6$ (`Rule30Submission.erosion3_fin`). Corollary: for every attachment column $a$ and width $b\ge1$, every $W$ with `WallOK a b W` is empty (`Rule30Submission.no_wall`). The period-3 ether has no wall of any width.

The catalog proved there is no wall of width $\le12$ (`Rule30EtherThreeNoWall.no_wall_le_12`) and nothing about how defects move on the ether. Now the ether-and-wall route (`absorption3_excludes`) cannot exclude `001` or `011` with any wall.

The method follows the leftmost defect, the *front*. Its state is the ether class of its column plus one bit: 24 states. A 576-case kernel check (`cert_all`, `front_step`) shows that only one state, $B$, can move the front $\ge3$ columns right. On the other 23, a potential $\psi\in[0,10]$ makes $5D+2t+\psi$ non-increasing (`wake_good`). For a finite perturbation the rightmost defect moves right exactly one column per step (`redge_step`), so runs of $B$ are short (`run_bad`).

Not claimed:
- erosion with an infinite right side, which is open and equivalent to "no infinite run of $B$";
- the measured worst case $3w+2$;
- the exact speed $2/5$;
- anything about `AbsorptionT`, `Q001`, `C3s001`, `C3w`, or Problems 2 and 3.

This supersedes nothing. Direct AI involvement: Primary submission credits Luis Perez Morales; Claude (Fable 5.1); agent disclosure: Claude Code with Claude Fable 5.1. Further checking: This is a bounded partial result only, not a solution to any Rule30 Prize problem. Registry explicitly reports human review and kit incorporation, but novelty and scope still require comparison with the dated prior kit. Compare overlapping word families, bound improvements and antecedents exactly; independently inspect the actual submission and finite certificate scope. Keep only the new scoped contribution, not known background or numerical observations.  Independently check correctness, novelty, priority, exact AI mathematical contribution and statement correspondence. Source-reported author/agent, kernel or registry checks are not an independent expert audit here; no downloaded proof artifact, certificate, program or macro was executed. Registry/submission dates are dated public observations; reconstruct any earlier public manuscript or artifact release before backdating. Retain provisional=1, low strict confidence, taxonomy unreviewed and no strict Superhuman override.

